// x-engine-seq-errors-02: when two sibling `mod` statements both fail to
// resolve, which error is reported is nondeterministic: resolve_children
// (graphix-types/src/expr/resolver.rs) uses try_join_all, which returns the
// first error to COMPLETE, not the first in program order.
// command (no files key.gx / user.gx beside this one):
//   for i in $(seq 30); do graphix --no-cache --check x-engine-seq-errors-02.gx 2>&1 | head -1; done | sort | uniq -c
// observed: 29x "line: 10 ... mod nosuch_key", 1x "line: 11 ... mod nosuch_user"
// (a sibling dir with only mod key; mod user: 28 vs 2; the rate varies with load)
// expected: always the first (line 10). The LSP republishes a different
// diagnostic on each check of an unchanged buffer.
mod nosuch_key;
mod nosuch_user;
0
